@page "/"

<PageTitle>Blaze</PageTitle>

<h1 id="header">Blaze</h1>
<h2 id="subheader">A Blazor-based management UI</h2>
<hr />

<h3>What is Blazor?</h3>
<p>
    Blazor is a web framework for .NET, used with the C# programming language. This framework is part of the ASP.NET Core web library and offers a suitable
    alternative to PHP. The *.razor files used by this framework combine HTML markup with C# code. Again, PHP uses a similar approach. While the C# code here
    is server-side, you can still write client-side code in JavaScript, just like you can with PHP files. Just type in your name below and click on the button.
    That alert that will come up is the only thing I wrote in JavaScript here.
</p>

<input id="nameInput" />

<button id="clickme">Click me</button>

<h3>What does Blaze have for management stuff?</h3>

<p>
    Blaze comes with the following:
</p>

<ul>
    <li>Genders</li>
    <li>People (sometimes referred to as characters too, sorry)</li>
    <li>Companies</li>
    <li>Social Media links for people and companies</li>
</ul>

<script type="text/javascript">
var button = document.getElementById("clickme");

button.addEventListener("click", function () {
    var nameInput = document.getElementById("nameInput");
    alert("Hello, " + nameInput.value);
});
</script>